        "body": "In this block, connect point 3 to a concrete example. Vivir is an infinitive in the Spanish -ir family. Its stem is viv-, and its present endings for yo, tú, and él are -o, -es, and -e.\n\nViv- plus -o makes yo vivo; plus -es makes tú vives; plus -e makes él vive. Escribir follows the same route: escribo, escribes, escribe. Read the example again, then explain it in your own words before you begin the task.\n\nPractice: Write two complete sentences that name the idea and give its example.\n\nCommon mistake: Do not repeat a label without explaining what it means."
